  "conclusions": [
    {
      "area": "Overall",
      "finding": "Fine-tuned SEA-LION English-first currently strongest candidate on reviewed conversations, including random shared examples; no final-ready reliability or independent human accuracy established."
    },
    {
      "area": "mT5",
      "finding": "Older mT5 remains a useful reference and can produce natural local replies. Newer variants do not automatically improve it; persistent failures concern role assignment,negation,availability,status,numbers and deadlines."
    },
    {
      "area": "Public adaptation and data volume",
      "finding": "Full-model public adaptation,span corruption,CoSEM/DailyDialog and small/full data trials completed. Larger public corpora do not consistently improve reply quality despite some lower losses."
    },
    {
      "area": "Task expansion and target repair/distillation",
      "finding": "190\u2192790 comparisons,repaired600generated examples and reviewed teacher targets tried. Target coherence and style matter; neither more synthetic data nor offline distillation established robust contextual improvement."
    },
    {
      "area": "English-first rewriting/shared and split adapters",
      "finding": "English anchors help intent consistency in some experiments. Rewriters can still change meaning, and preserving wrong English does not yield a correct pair."
    },
    {
      "area": "Full fine-tuning and LoRA",
      "finding": "Many LR,seed,duration and adapter-target variants tried; lower validation loss is not equivalent to better replies. No universally best mT5 variant established."
    },
    {
      "area": "Generation decoding",
      "finding": "Greedy,beam4,beam8 and no-repeat constraints tried. Some wording improves; plainSEAbeam can loop. No-repeat3 helps repetition but does not ensure factual correctness."
    },
    {
      "area": "Planning/reply acts/structured objectives",
      "finding": "Prompted large-model plans and trained mT5 classifier/conditioning/structured-task trials explored; no reliable end-to-end mT5 upgrade established."
    },
    {
      "area": "Unlikelihood/preferences/reward/RL pilots",
      "finding": "Unlikelihood,DPO/preference and constrained reward/structured-RL experiments are mixed or unreliable. Judge/scorer failures matter; this is not a completed successful general RLHF solution."
    },
    {
      "area": "Output head and small MLP",
      "finding": "Actual token-generator alternatives to LoRA completed.394kMLP English loss near separateLoRA, but rewrite loss/meaning failures persist;192Moutput-only head not an upgrade."
    },
    {
      "area": "Frozen linear diagnostic probes",
      "finding": "Availability/completion mostly near chance on reserved synthetic cases; ownership modest. Limited readouts do not prove facts absent and were not a generation-model replacement."
    },
    {
      "area": "180contextpairs",
      "finding": "No consistent context-pair benefit across the two tested seeds: worse macroCE in seed1, marginally better in seed2; role,negation,budget,time failures remain in reviewed newcases. Not proof all auxiliary ratios/budgets are ineffective."
    },
    {
      "area": "Rerankers",
      "finding": "BM25/MiniLM and teammate trainedQwen3-Reranker0.6B are separate components. No confirmed gain on current generator pools; ranking cannot supply absent good candidates."
    },
    {
      "area": "Not executed",
      "finding": "MoE-LoRA was discussed but has not been run. Research suggestions are not counted as completed experiments."
    }
  ],
